    <innerclass refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1Hello" prot="public">api::v2::Hello</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi">api</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2">api::v2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Minimal welcome endpoint used to confirm the API is reachable. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file defines the Hello controller with one tiny endpoint. When called it always sends back the same JSON greeting with status 200. It reads nothing from the request, touches no database and keeps no state, which makes it the simplest possible example of a Drogon route. Its main job is to act as a liveness check: if this endpoint answers, the server is up and the HTTP stack is working.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is the &quot;is the API alive?&quot; endpoint. Operators and automated health checks call it to confirm the server is running without needing a login or any data. Drogon serves it at /api/v2/hello through the INSECURE chain, so it is rate-limited and timed but requires no token. It calls JsonHelper to build the greeting; without it there would be no quick way to verify basic connectivity.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Health/liveness endpoint: a trivial URL used to check a service is running.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP GET: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Methods">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Methods</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP filters/middleware: <ulink url="https://drogon.docsforge.com/master/filter/">https://drogon.docsforge.com/master/filter/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CORS: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
